1
00:00:00,084 --> 00:00:01,292
<i>Previously on</i> Reacher...

2
00:00:01,293 --> 00:00:02,712
Hand over the drive, Reacher.

3
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:07,800
Gun!

4
00:00:10,970 --> 00:00:13,179
I got it. Move.

5
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:15,682
We got a GSW to the chest.

6
00:00:15,683 --> 00:00:17,392
He's one of the guys.

7
00:00:17,393 --> 00:00:19,310
Stop!
Get down! On the ground now!

8
00:00:19,311 --> 00:00:21,771
Jacob. Mother of God.

9
00:00:21,772 --> 00:00:24,399
- You're safe now, kid.
- Why are we idling, Monty?

10
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:25,525
I love you so much, Jakey.

11
00:00:25,526 --> 00:00:26,526
- It's for the best.
- No, no, no.

12
00:00:26,527 --> 00:00:27,944
- Please don't let them take me.
- Shut the fuck up.

13
00:00:27,945 --> 00:00:29,821
- I get locked up, they'll get to me.
- Shut the...

14
00:00:29,822 --> 00:00:31,489
How long until they figure out
it's all connected,

15
00:00:31,490 --> 00:00:32,949
to Indonesia and Anna Merrick?

16
00:00:32,950 --> 00:00:34,284
He's on the run.

17
00:00:34,285 --> 00:00:36,870
<i>His only option is
to go after the guy in that photo.</i>

18
00:00:36,871 --> 00:00:39,080
You find that man
and you'll find Jack Reacher.

19
00:00:39,081 --> 00:00:40,915
We need to speak
with Leo Ahlquist, please.

20
00:00:40,916 --> 00:00:42,292
I want to know what's on these servers,

21
00:00:42,293 --> 00:00:43,877
and how it's connected
to that photo you're in.

22
00:00:43,878 --> 00:00:45,420
- Don't move.
- So, the mercenaries

23
00:00:45,421 --> 00:00:47,922
- have been yours the whole time.
- You should've walked out

24
00:00:47,923 --> 00:00:50,592
of that police station
three days ago and left Philly.

25
00:00:50,593 --> 00:00:52,552
<i>Don't deal with them in the office.
Take them off-site.</i>

26
00:00:52,553 --> 00:00:55,139
They're gonna drive us deep into the woods
and then they're gonna kill us.

27
00:00:57,308 --> 00:00:58,309
Time to die.

28
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:16,993
No head shots.

29
00:01:16,994 --> 00:01:19,454
Less blood to clean.

30
00:01:22,374 --> 00:01:24,125
Hey, there.

31
00:01:24,126 --> 00:01:25,919
Can you guys help me out?

32
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:29,297
I-I've been trying to find the lake,
and I'm just lost as hell.

33
00:01:29,298 --> 00:01:31,758
Yeah, wrong way, pal.
This is private property.

34
00:01:31,759 --> 00:01:34,219
- Ah, man, I must have taken a bad turn.
- We got to warn him.

35
00:01:34,220 --> 00:01:37,138
- We shout, they'll kill him.
- This place is so confusing.

36
00:01:37,139 --> 00:01:38,890
Maybe he'll just leave.

37
00:01:38,891 --> 00:01:41,434
Just turn around,
go back the way you came.

38
00:01:41,435 --> 00:01:44,062
See, that's the thing,
I don't even know where the main road is.

39
00:01:44,063 --> 00:01:46,189
D-Do you mind taking a look
at my map for me?

40
00:01:46,190 --> 00:01:48,526
Yeah, sure. Let's take a look.

41
00:01:49,026 --> 00:01:50,527
No!

42
00:01:59,161 --> 00:02:00,745
Reacher. Ma'am.

43
00:02:00,746 --> 00:02:02,288
So, Sampson did know

44
00:02:02,289 --> 00:02:03,790
who was in that photo.

45
00:02:03,791 --> 00:02:05,501
Not till after you called.

46
00:02:06,335 --> 00:02:08,795
Did some checking with old sources,

47
00:02:08,796 --> 00:02:10,630
figured out it was Ahlquist.

48
00:02:10,631 --> 00:02:12,924
Sent me down here to talk to him.

49
00:02:12,925 --> 00:02:16,469
Showed up at his building to see
these guys load you two into a van,

50
00:02:16,470 --> 00:02:19,139
so... I followed.

51
00:02:21,725 --> 00:02:23,476
Unlock us.

52
00:02:23,477 --> 00:02:25,896
We have a conversation
to finish with Ahlquist.

53
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:01,599
End of the line.

54
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:18,990
- Let's go.
- No. Get-get off.

55
00:03:18,991 --> 00:03:20,409
Let's go.

56
00:03:21,702 --> 00:03:23,244
- All right.
- Okay.

57
00:03:23,245 --> 00:03:25,204
- Down there, around the corner.
- Listen. Listen to me.

58
00:03:25,205 --> 00:03:26,289
- Listen--
- I don't...

59
00:03:26,290 --> 00:03:27,916
just do what I fucking tell you.

60
00:03:27,917 --> 00:03:29,542
You don't have to do this.

61
00:03:41,847 --> 00:03:43,933
All right. That's better.

62
00:03:47,436 --> 00:03:49,021
Okay. Face me.

63
00:04:01,492 --> 00:04:02,909
Okay.

64
00:04:02,910 --> 00:04:04,620
Get out of here.

65
00:04:06,789 --> 00:04:08,456
I-I thought you were gonna kill me.

66
00:04:08,457 --> 00:04:11,793
What the hell
kind of cop you think I am?

67
00:04:11,794 --> 00:04:14,128
I don't know. What kind are you?

68
00:04:14,129 --> 00:04:16,714
The kind who almost
turned the car around three times

69
00:04:16,715 --> 00:04:18,508
to actually bring you in.

70
00:04:18,509 --> 00:04:20,510
- So why didn't you?
- Because of that guy

71
00:04:20,511 --> 00:04:22,720
whose ear Reacher ripped off.

72
00:04:22,721 --> 00:04:23,930
We thought he was on the job.

73
00:04:23,931 --> 00:04:25,431
Turns out,
no one could find him in the system.

74
00:04:25,432 --> 00:04:27,934
Next thing we know, these CIA assholes

75
00:04:27,935 --> 00:04:30,728
come to take him away,
tell us "it never happened."

76
00:04:30,729 --> 00:04:32,188
Real men in black shit.

77
00:04:32,189 --> 00:04:33,564
And that one-eared fuck,

78
00:04:33,565 --> 00:04:36,484
he had a tranquilizer gun
and a key to Reacher's cell.

79
00:04:36,485 --> 00:04:38,194
What does that sound like to you?

80
00:04:38,195 --> 00:04:39,570
That they were gonna murder him.

81
00:04:39,571 --> 00:04:42,574
So, what the hell has
my partner gotten herself into?

82
00:04:44,076 --> 00:04:47,370
It's... really complicated.

83
00:04:47,371 --> 00:04:49,747
Then speak slowly.

84
00:04:49,748 --> 00:04:52,917
The night my sister died,

85
00:04:52,918 --> 00:04:56,295
she had a jump drive with
sensitive government information on it.

86
00:04:56,296 --> 00:04:57,922
The thing that the Feds were looking for?

87
00:04:57,923 --> 00:04:59,924
They weren't the only ones who wanted it.

88
00:04:59,925 --> 00:05:02,468
These two Indonesian women, the CIA,

89
00:05:02,469 --> 00:05:04,053
some well-trained operatives.

90
00:05:04,054 --> 00:05:05,805
But we found it first.

91
00:05:05,806 --> 00:05:08,391
Is that how we got to that, uh,
shoot-out in that restaurant?

92
00:05:08,392 --> 00:05:09,559
Yeah.

93
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:11,394
The women wound up with it.

94
00:05:11,395 --> 00:05:12,812
Do you know what's on it?

95
00:05:12,813 --> 00:05:14,647
A decades-old photo.

96
00:05:14,648 --> 00:05:16,941
Tamara and Reacher went to talk
to one of the men in the picture,

97
00:05:16,942 --> 00:05:19,778
some, uh, chemist named Leo Ahlquist.

98
00:05:20,863 --> 00:05:22,071
Chemist?

99
00:05:22,072 --> 00:05:24,991
- What?
- We found a bunch of chemistry stuff

100
00:05:24,992 --> 00:05:28,536
at the restaurant,
like beakers and Bunsen burners and shit.

101
00:05:28,537 --> 00:05:30,414
Looked like someone was
planning on making something.

102
00:05:31,415 --> 00:05:32,832
That can't be good.

103
00:05:32,833 --> 00:05:34,459
So, where's this Ahlquist?

104
00:05:34,460 --> 00:05:35,710
Dover.

105
00:05:35,711 --> 00:05:37,128
It's a little out of my jurisdiction,

106
00:05:37,129 --> 00:05:40,173
but if she needs help in Philly,
tell her to call me.

107
00:05:40,174 --> 00:05:41,592
I'll do what I can.

108
00:05:42,676 --> 00:05:45,094
You know how Tamara ended up

109
00:05:45,095 --> 00:05:46,888
working with a clock-puncher like me?

110
00:05:46,889 --> 00:05:50,099
By insisting on doing the right thing.

111
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:53,479
You know, she's a pain in the ass,
but she's the most stand-up police I know.

112
00:05:54,063 --> 00:05:57,356
And I knew all that stuff they were saying
about her on the news was garbage.

113
00:05:57,357 --> 00:05:59,609
Are you gonna get in trouble for this?

114
00:05:59,610 --> 00:06:01,862
Not if I can help it.

115
00:06:05,407 --> 00:06:06,533
Hey.

116
00:06:06,992 --> 00:06:08,576
Okay. Right here.

117
00:06:08,577 --> 00:06:09,703
Just right here.

118
00:06:11,038 --> 00:06:13,372
- "Right here" what?
- Butt of the gun,

119
00:06:13,373 --> 00:06:16,167
right here where the skin is tight,
all right?

120
00:06:16,168 --> 00:06:18,211
The story will be you faked a seizure,

121
00:06:18,212 --> 00:06:20,129
I checked on you, you attacked,

122
00:06:20,130 --> 00:06:22,799
you headbutted me,
knocked me loopy and then escaped.

123
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:24,467
You got 15 years on me.

124
00:06:24,468 --> 00:06:26,969
They'll believe
that you got the jump on my old ass.

125
00:06:26,970 --> 00:06:29,722
Maybe I also ran off with the gun, too?

126
00:06:29,723 --> 00:06:31,516
No, don't press your luck, all right?

127
00:06:31,517 --> 00:06:34,811
I'm gonna be fucked enough over this
without losing my piece, all right?

128
00:06:34,812 --> 00:06:36,730
Let's do this. It's showtime, all right?

129
00:06:40,901 --> 00:06:42,819
- Ow, ah, oh.
- Ooh.

130
00:06:42,820 --> 00:06:44,529
- Okay, all right, all right, good, good.
- Okay. You okay?

131
00:06:44,530 --> 00:06:46,739
Good. Good work, good work.

132
00:06:46,740 --> 00:06:49,534
All right, now get moving,
keep your head down.

133
00:06:49,535 --> 00:06:51,410
Oh, can you do me a favor?

134
00:06:51,411 --> 00:06:54,247
I'm pretty sure
I'm doing you one right now.

135
00:06:54,248 --> 00:06:55,998
Check in on Russell Plum.

136
00:06:55,999 --> 00:06:57,834
GSW admitted to Penn Presby.

137
00:06:57,835 --> 00:06:58,752
Okay? Tell him...

138
00:06:59,837 --> 00:07:02,088
...I'm sorry I left him at the library.

139
00:07:02,089 --> 00:07:03,674
Yeah, sure.

140
00:07:05,717 --> 00:07:06,926
I don't know how to thank you.

141
00:07:06,927 --> 00:07:09,846
By getting the fuck out of here.
We're not friends now, all right?

142
00:07:09,847 --> 00:07:11,765
We're not having a moment here. Get lost.

143
00:07:22,025 --> 00:07:23,234
<i>The person
you have reached</i>

144
00:07:23,235 --> 00:07:25,319
<i>- is not available at this time.</i>
- You got to be fucking kidding me.

145
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:26,904
<i>Please leave a message.</i>

146
00:07:26,905 --> 00:07:29,282
Where the hell are you?

147
00:07:29,283 --> 00:07:30,783
I need confirmation

148
00:07:30,784 --> 00:07:32,411
you completed your assignment,
so we can--

149
00:08:02,399 --> 00:08:04,567
We never got to finish our talk.

150
00:08:26,548 --> 00:08:27,632
Ow!

151
00:08:29,551 --> 00:08:30,927
How did you find me?

152
00:08:30,928 --> 00:08:32,345
I saw how many hard drives
you had to shred,

153
00:08:32,346 --> 00:08:34,805
so I waited outside your office
till you were done and tailed you.

154
00:08:34,806 --> 00:08:36,641
I can get you money. You want money?

155
00:08:36,642 --> 00:08:38,684
- I'll get you money.
- I want answers.

156
00:08:38,685 --> 00:08:40,269
What's in that photograph
that's so important

157
00:08:40,270 --> 00:08:42,689
you and everyone else
are willing to kill for it?

158
00:08:45,067 --> 00:08:47,027
Remember how I said
I was gonna make you talk?

159
00:08:48,278 --> 00:08:49,946
No, no, n--

160
00:08:49,947 --> 00:08:51,822
Goddamn it!

161
00:08:51,823 --> 00:08:53,658
Fuck!

162
00:08:53,659 --> 00:08:55,993
No, no, no! Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

163
00:08:55,994 --> 00:08:58,537
I'll tell... I'll tell you anything
you want to know. Don't...

164
00:08:58,538 --> 00:09:00,122
The photograph.

165
00:09:01,333 --> 00:09:03,084
It contains the formula

166
00:09:03,085 --> 00:09:05,503
for a chemical
weapon of mass destruction.

167
00:09:05,504 --> 00:09:07,255
There's no formula in the photograph.

168
00:09:07,256 --> 00:09:08,965
It's there. You just can't see it.

169
00:09:10,300 --> 00:09:11,968
- Start making sense!
- Okay, okay.

170
00:09:11,969 --> 00:09:13,719
Let me explain.

171
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:14,930
Get to it.

172
00:09:18,642 --> 00:09:22,812
After the '95 sarin gas attacks
on the Tokyo subway,

173
00:09:22,813 --> 00:09:25,731
the U.S. figured that chemical weapons

174
00:09:25,732 --> 00:09:29,278
would be the next WMD of choice
for the world's worst terrorists...

175
00:09:30,362 --> 00:09:33,322
...so the CIA secretly contracted DARPA.

176
00:09:33,323 --> 00:09:35,157
I was working there,

177
00:09:35,158 --> 00:09:38,452
an assistant, just out of grad school.

178
00:09:38,453 --> 00:09:41,247
They assigned me to a project,
Operation Mongoose.

179
00:09:41,248 --> 00:09:44,000
We were supposed to create
chemical weapons

180
00:09:44,001 --> 00:09:46,210
and then reverse engineer them

181
00:09:46,211 --> 00:09:48,296
to find antidotes and countermeasures.

182
00:09:48,297 --> 00:09:52,425
Geneva Protocol and Chemical
Weapons Convention outlawed them.

183
00:09:54,094 --> 00:09:56,053
It was all off the books.

184
00:09:56,054 --> 00:09:59,223
An Indonesian Army general named Putra

185
00:09:59,224 --> 00:10:03,352
was trying to get the U.S. Special Forces
to come and train his men for a while.

186
00:10:03,353 --> 00:10:08,399
Now, Putra was sketchy, but Washington
saw an opportunity to cut a deal.

187
00:10:08,400 --> 00:10:10,151
In exchange for training,

188
00:10:10,152 --> 00:10:11,902
Putra would allow the CIA to build

189
00:10:11,903 --> 00:10:14,280
a secret chemical weapons lab
in the rainforest.

190
00:10:14,281 --> 00:10:15,990
John Sampson knew about this?

191
00:10:15,991 --> 00:10:17,992
No.
We were told to keep it from Sampson

192
00:10:17,993 --> 00:10:19,619
and the guys under him.

193
00:10:21,288 --> 00:10:22,706
Stay low.

194
00:10:24,124 --> 00:10:25,584
Stay low.

195
00:10:26,877 --> 00:10:28,419
Stay low.

196
00:10:30,422 --> 00:10:33,049
Stay low. Stay low.

197
00:10:33,050 --> 00:10:35,134
Move, move, move.

198
00:10:35,135 --> 00:10:36,802
<i>Sampson was a Boy Scout.</i>

199
00:10:36,803 --> 00:10:38,888
<i>If he'd known we were breaking
international law,</i>

200
00:10:38,889 --> 00:10:40,306
<i>he'd have blown the whistle.</i>

201
00:10:40,307 --> 00:10:42,684
<i>He thought we were there
doing malaria research.</i>

202
00:10:43,685 --> 00:10:46,520
<i>The only Delta guy
who knew what we were really doing</i>

203
00:10:46,521 --> 00:10:49,274
<i>was their commanding officer, Cahill.</i>

204
00:10:53,070 --> 00:10:54,737
He helped us cover it up.

205
00:10:54,738 --> 00:10:57,239
So, that's why Cahill was
on the subway that night?

206
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:59,867
- Still trying to bury all this?
- Yes.

207
00:10:59,868 --> 00:11:01,827
When that clerk Merrick
stole the Delta files,

208
00:11:01,828 --> 00:11:04,206
she must have tripped
some alarm in the system.

209
00:11:13,799 --> 00:11:17,552
<i>The Department of Defense
sent some of their guys to follow her...</i>

210
00:11:18,470 --> 00:11:20,097
<i>...see where she was taking
the stolen info.</i>

211
00:11:22,307 --> 00:11:25,060
<i>They picked up her trail
a few blocks from work.</i>

212
00:11:25,560 --> 00:11:29,564
<i>They figured it was low-level stuff,
since it was from Indonesia in '98.</i>

213
00:11:30,690 --> 00:11:33,234
<i>They had no idea
what that photo could unleash.</i>

214
00:11:35,654 --> 00:11:38,989
<i>They called Sampson's office
as a courtesy.</i>

215
00:11:38,990 --> 00:11:40,866
<i>It was late.</i>

216
00:11:40,867 --> 00:11:43,369
<i>- Cahill was the only one there.</i>
- Cahill.

217
00:11:43,370 --> 00:11:45,454
<i>He knew, if those files were
being targeted,</i>

218
00:11:45,455 --> 00:11:48,082
<i>there must have been
something incriminating in it.</i>

219
00:11:48,083 --> 00:11:51,127
<i>It didn't take him long
to realize what it was.</i>

220
00:11:51,128 --> 00:11:53,546
Cahill caught up with the Feds
tailing Merrick,

221
00:11:53,547 --> 00:11:56,382
he cut them off,
made them get into a fender bender

222
00:11:56,383 --> 00:11:59,135
on the highway so they lost her scent.

223
00:11:59,136 --> 00:12:02,139
Feds never saw him,
and he kept on Anna's tail.

224
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:05,349
<i>He was Delta.</i>

225
00:12:05,350 --> 00:12:07,518
<i>That kind of stuff was in his wheelhouse.</i>

226
00:12:07,519 --> 00:12:10,104
<i>He tracked her all the way to the subway.</i>

227
00:12:10,105 --> 00:12:13,774
<i>He was gonna take the drive from her
as soon as he got her alone.</i>

228
00:12:13,775 --> 00:12:15,777
<i>Then everything went to hell.</i>

229
00:12:17,696 --> 00:12:19,697
But you know that part, don't you?

230
00:12:21,867 --> 00:12:25,161
So, when the cops came,
Cahill slipped out and called to warn you.

231
00:12:25,162 --> 00:12:26,579
He made two calls.

232
00:12:26,580 --> 00:12:28,497
One to me and one to Foster,

233
00:12:28,498 --> 00:12:32,042
the CIA officer
who ran Operation Mongoose.

234
00:12:32,043 --> 00:12:34,879
I know Foster. I ripped his ear off.

235
00:12:34,880 --> 00:12:37,006
Calling Foster makes sense,

236
00:12:37,007 --> 00:12:40,134
'cause Cahill wanted whatever was on
that drive to never see the light of day,

237
00:12:40,135 --> 00:12:43,554
and Cahill figured that the CIA gave them
the best chance of doing that quietly.

238
00:12:43,555 --> 00:12:45,348
But why call you?

239
00:12:46,349 --> 00:12:48,185
Like you said,
you were just an assistant.

240
00:12:52,647 --> 00:12:54,274
Snap that shit.

241
00:12:55,317 --> 00:12:56,609
No! No! No!

242
00:12:56,610 --> 00:12:59,570
He called because I was using
what we learned in the jungle,

243
00:12:59,571 --> 00:13:00,988
and Cahill knew that.

244
00:13:00,989 --> 00:13:02,157
How did he know?

245
00:13:03,158 --> 00:13:06,452
Uh, after I made billions off pesticides,
when my company grew,

246
00:13:06,453 --> 00:13:09,163
my name was in the press a lot

247
00:13:09,164 --> 00:13:11,624
and Cahill recognized me from Indonesia.

248
00:13:11,625 --> 00:13:13,584
He reached out years ago,

249
00:13:13,585 --> 00:13:17,546
